  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 154 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nLingering wrap around rain showers are expected to continue with-in \nthe deformation zone over central and eastern Kansas today. The rain \nwill begin to taper off by later this afternoon as the upper wave \nmoves northeast into Iowa. Dry weather is slated for Wednesday with \nnear normal daytime highs. Meanwhile current satellite water vapor \nimagery shows a healthy upper level PV wave approaching northern \nCalifornia in the eastern Pacific. Deterministic and ensemble models \nare showing a intensifying trend with this system and a deeper warm \nadvection signal. Instability looks to be limited therefore \nexpecting mainly rain showers. The rain will begin over western \nKansas Wednesday night and spread eastward affecting mainly south \ncentral/southeast Kansas during the day on Thursday. \n\nA dry weather pattern will be in store for the region on Friday \nthrough the weekend as upper level ridging builds over Kansas on \nFriday. Models do show a upper trough quickly pivoting across the \nregion for Saturday, but limited moisture and weakening trend of \nthis upper trough favors dry weather conditions. Daytime highs will \ncontinue to be around seasonal averages for early November.",
